rs/andrew-weisman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andrew-weisman","id":44007191,"login":"andrew-weisman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDA3MTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrew-weisman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CBIIT/multiplex-analysis-web-apps/commits/aee6cd20bdc60cc05f1fcdf89d22c5b770c413b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-02T04:57:21Z","email":"andrew.weisman@nih.gov","name":"Andrew Weisman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-02T04:57:21Z","email":"andrew.weisman@nih.gov","name":"Andrew Weisman"},"message":"Add \"raise\" to some except blocks (as we should do in general), and more importantly, reconstruct lazyframes separately after (1) session state is read in and (2) rest of the special objects are reconstructed. Simplify the code accordingly, which shows that this is probably the correct approach (simplify parameters for example... simple is usually better). Further, implement topological sort to ensure that when the lazyframes are reconstructed, they will do so in order of the components that matter, so e.g. we never have to worry about making sure to step through the pages sequentially.","tree":{"sha":"02db2cd9868ee6b2f1016879e30ad5645f0c18b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CBIIT/multiplex-analysis-web-apps/git