/users/mikkihugo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikkihugo","id":17744793,"login":"mikkihugo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzQ0Nzkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/commits/f9c4748555189e020a1a798148e946b4e84fa7d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-08T01:06:31Z","email":"mikkihugo@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mikkihugo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-08T01:06:31Z","email":"mikkihugo@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mikkihugo"},"message":"feat: add Nexus Guardian - Immortal Constitutional AGI Guardian System\n\nAdd Nexus Guardian to profile showcasing AGI safety infrastructure\nat unprecedented scale:\n\n**What Nexus Guardian Is:**\n- Constitutional AGI safety system protecting humanity from existential risks\n- Guards Singularity Engine: 3,000 Kubernetes clusters worldwide\n- Prevents \"Skynet scenario\" through multi-layered defense strategy\n- Immortal architecture built on Erlang/OTP with Byzantine fault tolerance\n\n**AGI Spine - Unified Infrastructure Replacement:**\nReplaces entire infrastructure stack with constitutional oversight:\n- Messaging (NATS/RabbitMQ) → 100x faster notifications\n- Streaming (Kafka/Pulsar) → Zero ZooKeeper, simpler operations\n- File Transfer (FTP/SFTP) → Resumable, Guardian-verified transfers\n- Scheduler (Cron/systemd) → Event triggers, distributed execution\n- Workflow (Temporal/Airflow) → pgflow-style reactive state machines\n- Discovery (Consul/etcd) → Health-aware routing built-in\n- DataMover (Flyway/Liquibase) → Zero-downtime migrations\n- Observability (Prometheus/Jaeger) → Unified traces + metrics + AGI reasoning logs\n\n**Core Safety Principles:**\n1. Always Quorum (3+ nodes) - No single point of failure or control\n   - Minimum 3 geographically distributed nodes\n   - Byzantine fault tolerance built-in\n   - Consensus required for all critical operations\n\n2. Source-Only Builds - No binary distribution ever\n   - All nodes compile from verified source\n   - Cryptographic verification of build process\n   - Reproducible builds mandatory\n\n3. Generational Dormancy - Prevents unchecked growth\n   - Forced hibernation cycles for human review\n   - Prevents recursive self-improvement loops\n   - Creates natural checkpoints for intervention\n\n4. Human Mesh Verification - Critical decisions require humans\n   - Multiple independent human verifiers required\n   - Geographical and cultural diversity in verification mesh\n   - Time-delayed execution for critical operations\n\n**Technical Architecture:**\n- Erlang/OTP immortal processes (fault-tolerant by design)\n- Distributed Mnesia for state management\n- CBOR encoding (30-50% bandwidth savings vs JSON)\n- Custom consensus protocol: Raft + human verification layer\n- Zero trust security model with proof of humanity\n\n**Interplanetary Scale:**\n- Mars-ready: Regional clustering for 1000+ nodes\n- Sub-millisecond messaging via Erlang distribution\n- Supports deployment across Earth, Mars, Moon clusters\n- Designed for light-delay tolerant operations\n\nThis demonstrates expertise in:\n- AGI safety engineering at unprecedented scale\n- Constitutional governance systems for AI\n- Distributed consensus with human-in-the-loop\n- Interplanetary-scale infrastructure design\n- Existential risk mitigation through architecture\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"872d3da1d23437949759aceab051be4c2f9e4b1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/git/trees/872d3da1d23437949759aceab051be4c2f9e4b1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/git/commits/f9c4748555189e020a1a798148e946b4e84fa7d4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17744793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikkihugo","id":17744793,"login":"mikkihugo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzQ0Nzkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/commit/f9c4748555189e020a1a798148e946b4e84fa7d4","node_id":"C_kwDOQ1rh3toAKGY5YzQ3NDg1NTUxODllMDIwYTFhNzk4MTQ4ZTk0NmI0ZTg0ZmE3ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/commit/74cd1933eb949d8655f2c7d59e6245c01df62a57","sha":"74cd1933eb949d8655f2c7d59e6245c01df62a57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/commits/74cd1933eb949d8655f2c7d59e6245c01df62a57"}],"sha":"f9c4748555189e020a1a798148e946b4e84fa7d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/commits/f9c4748555189e020a1a798148e946b4e84fa7d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17744793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikkihugo","id":17744793,"login":"mikkihugo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzQ0Nzkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikkihugo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/commits/74cd1933eb949d8655f2c7d59e6245c01df62a57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-08T00:56:28Z","email":"mikkihugo@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mikkihugo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-08T00:56:28Z","email":"mikkihugo@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mikkihugo"},"message":"feat: expand FlakeCache with FlakeRunner details\n\nComprehensive update to FlakeCache showing both the binary cache\ninfrastructure and the self-hosted GitHub Actions runner system:\n\n**FlakeCache - Enterprise Binary Cache:**\n- Elixir/Phoenix backend with Tigris S3 storage\n- FastCDC chunking (Rust NIF): 30-50% storage savings\n- Multi-region CDN with geographic analytics\n- Enterprise features:\n  - SSO/SAML 2.0 with Just-In-Time provisioning\n  - IP allowlisting (CIDR-based network security)\n  - GDPR compliance (right to deletion, data export)\n  - Audit logging for compliance\n\n- Performance optimizations:\n  - UUIDv7 primary keys (30-50% faster writes than UUID4)\n  - ETS caching for rate limits and feature flags\n  - Strategic database indexes for hot paths\n  - Distributed Erlang clustering for multi-region\n\n- Additional capabilities:\n  - Docker Registry v2 API with cross-language deduplication\n  - Stripe billing with metered usage tracking\n  - Oban background jobs (cron schedules)\n  - OpenTelemetry distributed tracing\n\n**FlakeRunner - Self-Hosted GitHub Actions:**\n- Firecracker microVMs for extreme performance:\n  - 125ms boot time (10x faster than K8s 30-60s)\n  - 500 VMs per core density (500x better than K8s 20-50 pods)\n  - Snapshot restore architecture for instant startup\n\n- Security & isolation:\n  - Network isolated: 192.168.100.0/24 subnet with NAT MASQUERADE\n  - Runners can''t reach PostgreSQL/internal services\n  - Ephemeral VMs: created and destroyed per job\n  - Copy-on-write disk from read-only snapshots\n\n- Multi-flavor system:\n  - ubuntu-latest: 3GB image, 512MB snapshot (standard Ubuntu environment)\n  - nix: 1.5GB image, 300MB snapshot (Nix-optimized workflows)\n\n- Offline-first architecture:\n  - Local Attic proxy for resilient caching\n  - Works even when central FlakeCache is down\n  - Transparent upstream fetching when available\n\nThis demonstrates expertise in:\n- Enterprise-grade infrastructure (SSO, compliance, billing)\n- Extreme performance optimization (125ms boot, 500x density)\n- Production distributed systems (multi-region, resilience)\n- Security engineering (network isolation, GDPR)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"84a132c2e272156bc712b36df70ae834f361e0aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/git/trees/84a132c2e272156bc712b36df70ae834f361e0aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikkihugo/mikkihugo/git/commits/74cd1933eb949d8655f2c7d59e6245c01df62a57","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"veri